# The frontend image builds from ./frontend as its context, so the repo-root .dockerignore
# does NOT apply here — this file is what keeps host artefacts out of the image.
#
# node_modules is the load-bearing entry. The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` inside the image; if a
# host node_modules is copied in on top of it (as happens the moment anyone runs `npm install`
# locally for their IDE), the host's binaries — built for the host platform and carrying host
# permissions — clobber the container's, and `npm run build` dies with exit 126 (permission
# denied). Ignoring it also makes the build context small and the COPY layer cache-friendly.
node_modules
.next
out

.env*.local
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
